<title>UK: B.A.T off on worries about legal battle.</title>
<headline>B.A.T off on worries about legal battle.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries Plc extended their recent decline amid worries about the company's latest legal battle with the state of New York, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0919 GMT, the shares were off 6p to 478 on 1.3 million shares, making them among the most actively traded shares in London so far today.  </p>
<p>The company on Monday dismissed the lawsuit, which accuses tobacco companies of deceiving New Yorkers about the dangers of</p>
<p>Yet its shares have suffered, falling 11-1/2p yesterday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the market is still reeling from that suit,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>&quot;The problem is that there are no buyers around,&quot; said another.</p>
